 75NI    75CO B- DECAY:26.5 US:XUNDL-5 2021ES05                           202308
 75NI c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2021Es05:                          
 75NI2c  Phys Rev C 103, 064328 (2021)                                          
 75NI c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), February 3, 2022                      
 75NI c  2021Es05: {+75}Co source was produced via in-flight fission of E=345   
 75NI2c  MeV {+238}U beam from the RIKEN accelerator complex on a 3-mm-thick    
 75NI3c  {+9}Be target. Fragments were separated by the BigRIPS magnetic        
 75NI4c  spectrometer, selected by |DE-B|r-tof method, and transported through  
 75NI5c  the Zero-Degree spectrometer (ZDS) to the decay station. Charged       
 75NI6c  particles were detected with the WAS3ABi silicon array consisting of 8 
 75NI7c  layers of 1-mm-thick DSSSDs and |g rays were detected with the EURICA  
 75NI8c  array consisting of 84 HPGe crystals. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,    
 75NI9c  |b|g-coin, |g(t). Deduced levels, J, |p, branching ratios, log {Ift}.  
 75NIac  Comparisons with theoretical calculations.                             
 75NI c  Level scheme is constructed by 2021Es05 based on |g|g-coin data.       
 75NI c  I|b,log| {Ift}$ As given in 2021Es05. Quoted values are considered as  
 75NI2c  upper or lower limits for %I|b and log {Ift}, respectively, due to the 
 75NI3c  large Pandemonium effect (2021Es05).                                   
 75NI cG E,RI$From 2021Es05.                                                    
 75NI cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies (by compiler)            
 75NI cL J$As given in 2021Es05                                                 
